wideband: companion for everything above 16k, holding or not

The auto-wideband gate only saw the held rate, so with the holding off
the rates above sixteen thousand synthesised outright and dull, and
forty-eight thousand was refused outright. The gate reads the wanted
rate now: sixteen thousand itself stays native outright, everything
above takes the companion, whatever the holding says.
diff --git a/src/eci/synth/eci_synthwork.c b/src/eci/synth/eci_synthwork.c
index 80aa213..0b1c6e4 100644
--- a/src/eci/synth/eci_synthwork.c
+++ b/src/eci/synth/eci_synthwork.c
@@ -640,8 +640,14 @@ THIS int32_t stw_createAudioConverter(SynthThread *t, SampleFormat *fmt)
     /* The wideband voice engages by itself for anything above sixteen
        thousand: that is exactly where the checkbox used to engage it, since
        sixteen thousand itself is native outright and never took the
-       companion. No setting; the rate the caller asked for decides. */
-    wide = native == RATE_11025 && wanted > RATE_16000;
+       companion. No setting; the rate the caller asked for decides,
+       whatever the holding says -- with it off the engine would otherwise
+       synthesise these rates outright and dull, and forty-eight thousand,
+       past what it synthesises outright at all, comes back as nought.
+       Sixteen thousand itself stays native outright. */
+    wide = wanted > RATE_16000;
+    if (native == 0 && !wide)
+        return ERR_BAD_RATE;
     if (wide)
         native = WIDE_RATE;
 
